From 9775bcd31559726f8ab344088faf7cf3e2f11927 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ttabouch12 <ttabouch12@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:12:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 14/21] clk: samsung: exynos7870: Add CPU cluster clocks

Add CMU_CPUCL0 (0x10900000) and CMU_CPUCL1 (0x10800000) with their PLL1417x
cluster PLLs, switch user muxes and the CPU clock, plus the CMU_MIF
CPUCL{0,1}_SWITCH dividers and gates that provide the alternate parent used
while the cluster PLL relocks.

The PLL rate table covers the 15 frequencies (343 - 1794 MHz) of the vendor
DVFS table. Register offsets are taken from the vendor CAL code
(S5E7870-cmusfr.h, S5E7870-cmu.c).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01C7LhHXPfaxZf24zPigwQ9z
---
 drivers/clk/samsung/clk-exynos7870.c | 205 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 205 insertions(+)

